        "title": "feat(android): render LaTeX display math in chat via bundled KaTeX",
        "body": "Related: #100699\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nDelivers the declared Android math follow-up: `$$…$$` and `\\[…\\]` blocks in assistant responses rendered as typeset math instead of raw TeX, matching the iOS display-math behavior from #100829.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nDependency decision first: jlatexmath-android (the only native Android LaTeX library lineage) is GPL-2.0 and archived since 2023 — unusable for store distribution. Instead, KaTeX v0.17.0 (MIT) ships as bundled assets (minified js/css + required woff2 fonts only; no Gradle dependency): the release archive's SHA-256 matches GitHub's published digest, per-file hashes are recorded in an assets README, and the licenses screen gains a KaTeX entry (MIT + SIL OFL font note) per the Android licenses policy.\n\nRendering keeps WebViews out of the transcript entirely: one process-singleton offscreen WebView (attached as a transparent 1px view per Android's visible-state contract, lifecycle-detached) renders queued math jobs into bitmaps that transcript rows display as plain `Image`s, cached in a byte-bounded LRU keyed by latex/width/dark-mode, with negative caching and a 3s per-job timeout falling back to code-style raw text. The WebView is locked down: an asset-allowlist request interceptor returns empty responses for anything not under `file:///android_asset/katex/`, LaTeX reaches KaTeX only as a JSON-encoded `evaluateJavascript` argument (never HTML concatenation) with `trust:false`, `throwOnError:false`, `maxExpand:1000`, and the only JS bridge is a render-completion callback. Segmentation mirrors the iOS contract exactly: top-level blocks only, never inside code, unclosed math stays plain while streaming, 5000-byte cap falls back.\n\n## User Impact\n\nAndroid users see typeset display math in finished assistant messages; streaming, code blocks, and oversized/invalid math keep today's plain-text behavior. Android's licenses screen credits KaTeX.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- 37 tests green across segmenter (25: delimiters, code protection, streaming, caps), renderer protocol (8: queue ordering/dedupe, cache keying incl. dark mode, negative results, timeout fallback — WebView bridge injectable), and license notices (4).\n- Blacksmith Testbox focused run: BUILD SUCCESSFUL, exit 0; Play + ThirdParty Kotlin compile green; ktlint clean; `corepack pnpm native:i18n:sync` run.\n- Asset integrity: archive digest `f77cf2…4b88` matches GitHub's published release digest (independently re-verified via the releases API); per-file sha256s in `assets/katex/README.md`.\n- Structured review (codex) — clean.\n- Unverified: real-device pixel rendering (the renderer seam is injectable and covered; visual pass needs an authorized device install).\n",
